SUMMARY:Davis High Theater Presents: The Tragedy of Macbeth
DESCRIPTION:If you knew you were destined for power\, would you let fate take its course or would you grab destiny by the wheel and hit the gas?\nWhen three mysterious witches awaken Macbeth’s hunger for power\, ambition sets in motion a bloody chain of betrayal\, murder\, and madness. Shakespeare’s iconic\, haunting tragedy explores the dangerous consequences of mistaking destiny for something we can control. \nLocation\nBrunelle Theater @ 315 W 14th Street. \nPerformances\nFriday\, October 16\, Saturday October 17\, Friday October 23\, Saturday October 24 @7:00PM\nSunday October 18 and Sunday October 25 @2:00PM \nTickets\n$15 general admission\, $10 for DJUSD students\, and $5 on Sundays for DJUSD students.\nYou can buy your tickets online at https://sites.google.com/view/davishightheatre/home \nWe also encourage bringing cash for concessions ($2 each) to avoid an online fee. \nWe hope to see you there! \nAny questions\, please contact\nShenandoah Kehoe\nskehoe@djusd.net \nImage courtesy of Chad Fisk\nJoseph Martin as Macbeth
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/davis-high-theater-presents-the-tragedy-of-macbeth/2026-10-16/
LOCATION:Richard Brunelle Performance Hall\, 315 W 14th Street\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art,Community,Stage & Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/IMG_8013-rotated.jpeg
