SUMMARY:Indivisible Yolo’s No Kings Vote Early Events
DESCRIPTION:Indivisible Yolo will host three No Kings Vote Early events across Davis\, West Sacramento and Woodland on Oct. 17. The mass participation events will build upon the energy of previous mass protests as the group works to turn protest power into early voter action. Local residents are invited to attend one or more of the three community events and bring their ballots to submit. Hosted information booths will provide voter assistance\, including voter registration\, details on when and where to vote\, as well as information on California ballot initiatives and efforts to combat voter suppression. \nThe Woodland No Kings Vote Early event will take place from 10am-1pm at the Old Courthouse\, 725 Court Street. The West Sacramento event will take place from 10am-2pm at Trinity Presbyterian Church\, 1500 Park Boulevard. The Davis event will take place from 2-4pm at G Street Plaza\, 301 G Street. To sign up for one or more events\, visit https://www.indivisibleyolo.org/no-kings-vote-early. \nIndivisible Yolo is the local chapter of the nationwide grassroots movement Indivisible. Indivisible Yolo’s mission is to promote progressive policies by activating people to engage in their democracy at all levels of government. The group organizes and advocates for policy goals and to get out the vote to elect candidates who pursue those policies. These complementary efforts ensure democracy works for everyone and that those in power do\, too. For more information: www.indivisibleyolo.org.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/indivisible-yolos-no-kings-vote-early-events/
LOCATION:G Street Plaza\, Davis\, CA
CATEGORIES:Bring the Kids,Community,Outside
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/IY-No-Kings-2-October-2025-scaled.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Indivisible Yolo":MAILTO:indivisibleyolo@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
